  "status_text": "This morning we set a target for how much wiring it would take to answer all 1,024 questions on one grid. A circuit now fits that target. On the 32 by 32 grid, at most 201 AND/OR gates, each reading at most two earlier wires, give the right answer when one row and one column are on (L-meta-25492). A separate check matches every entry to the four-round rule that generated the grid (L-meta-25493). The 201 is an upper bound.",
